  "synthetic": true,
  "purpose": "Изолированные арифметические входы и выходы. Здесь нет транскриптов, conversation_id или оценок реальных диалогов.",
  "rule_source": {
    "filename": "CQA_Chat_Quality_Checklist 1.pdf",
    "pages": [
      1,
      2
    ]
  },
  "format_notes": [
    "Each input.checklist_ref resolves to a complete configuration in this file's checklists object.",
    "The criteria are a minimal projection of the shared checklist contract, sufficient for arithmetic only; semantic instructions are intentionally absent.",
    "All answers must match the selected configuration's allowed_answers, with exactly one answer per criterion.",
    "na excludes that criterion's weight and points. It is valid only when na_allowed=true; these fixtures do not test semantic applicability.",
    "kind=flag is excluded from all weighted calculations, even when its answer is yes; its weight is null.",
    "For binary: ratio(yes)=1 and ratio(no)=0. For scale: ratio=answer/scale_max; the answer must be one of the listed discrete values.",
    "Sum applicable weights and sum(weight*ratio) over non-flag, non-na criteria. If the weight sum is zero, total_score=null; otherwise total_score=100*weighted_points_before_normalization/applicable_weight.",
    "Round the final total only. Zero weights are allowed in the explicitly synthetic configuration used to exercise the denominator-zero case.",
    "gross_error is true exactly when the answer to the configured gross-error flag 08 is yes. This output does not impose a score penalty.",
    "A total_score JSON number such as 95.5 represents the rounded value 95.50; numeric trailing zeros are not significant."
  ],
  "rounding": {
    "decimal_places": 2,
    "mode": "ROUND_HALF_UP",
    "status": "implementation_choice_for_exact_ties",
    "note": "PDF requires rounding the final result to two decimals but does not specify the exact-half tie rule. Use Decimal and this explicit convention for these fixtures."
  },
